00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:54.300
And the sample library has
our Nginx template already.

00:14:54.300 --> 00:15:00.240
So if you click on this, you
can go to this Nginx overview

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:04.170
and preview what the
dashboard looks like.

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:06.480
Here, we're going to
skip that and just import

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:08.010
the sample dashboard.

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:12.700
So it will automatically
create a dashboard for you.

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:18.570
It has a few metrics
that's tracking already.

00:15:18.570 --> 00:15:22.140
And you can show
that it's tracking

00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:25.860
the few VMs we created before.

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:31.800
And it shows the total requests
coming to the Nginx server.

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:33.720
It shows the
current connections.

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:38.040
It also shows the history
of the connections.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:43.320
And of course, you can
also edit this dashboard

00:15:43.320 --> 00:15:46.620
or add more charts
to this dashboard,

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:53.430
because Nginx does ingest more
than just these three metrics.

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:57.000
On the other side, we mentioned
before that Ops Agent also

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:59.280
collects some system metrics.

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:06.510
So the most interesting one
might be the processes metrics.

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:12.690
If we go to the dashboard
list, there is GCP dashboard,

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:16.560
and one of them
says VM Instances.

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:19.950
If we go to this
page, it shows you

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:25.710
our few tabs of different
property of the VMs.

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:32.640
You can see CPU metrics, memory
metrics, and most excitingly,

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:35.280
you can see processes metrics.

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:38.880
They will tell you the
top processes by memory,

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:40.680
the top processes by CPU.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:43.950
So that way, we can
easily tell what

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:46.110
is using all the
resources on the VM

00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:48.150
and what could
potentially go wrong.

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:53.160
That's the dashboard part.

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:57.570
Now let's go back to see if
that execution of playbook--

00:16:57.570 --> 00:16:59.520
OK, it looks great.

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:03.120
The execution of the
playbook was successful.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:07.780
And that's actually
the end of this demo.

00:17:07.780 --> 00:17:09.002
Thank you so much.

